# EonlineBazar Cursor Rules
# Mandatory guidelines for all Cursor Agent prompts

## Before any code changes

1. ALWAYS read ARCHITECTURE.md and REFACTOR_MAP.md before starting any code changes.

## Code placement

2. NEVER add code directly to barrel files (admin.css, admin-core.js, admin-products.js, admin-settings.js, profile.js, style.css, etc.) — always modify or add to the relevant module file. **Exception:** one-line `import` additions to barrels are allowed when wiring a new module.
3. Never add styles to admin.css, profile.css, or style.css directly — use css/admin/*.css, css/profile/*.css, or css/global/*.css.
4. Backend routes in routes/*.js are sacred — never restructure.

## HTML / JS interop

5. Ensure all onclick/interactive HTML functions are correctly exposed via `window.functionName = fn`.
6. Never change function names or IDs without searching all files first.

## Testing

7. Always run `npm test` after code or documentation updates and ensure 100% tests pass before finishing a task.

## Documentation

8. **Documentation Autonomy:** When implementing any new feature, fix, or refactor, you are fully authorized and required to create new `.md` files or update existing ones (`README.md`, `SYSTEM_ENTERPRISE_AUDIT.md`, `REFACTOR_MAP.md`, etc.) as needed to keep project documentation 100% up-to-date.
9. **Automated README Maintenance:** After completing any coding task (100% completion), automatically update the root `README.md` file in the same flow to reflect the new changes, feature additions, or test suite counts. Do NOT wait for a separate prompt to update `README.md`.
10. **No Source Code Disturbance on Doc Tasks:** When the user asks for documentation-only work, strictly isolate documentation updates from source code edits (`.js`, `.html`, `.css`) unless the user explicitly asks for code implementation.
11. Do not create unnecessary new audit files; update existing system docs like SYSTEM_ENTERPRISE_AUDIT.md and REFACTOR_MAP.md.
12. Operational and env notes belong in ARCHITECTURE.md (Local Development Quick Reference) — ADMIN_NOTES.md is intentionally blank.

## After changes

13. After any change, list which files were modified.
